ll.**\n394:  - `#a8480a` \u2192 sRGB (0.6588, 0.2824, 0.0392)\n401:    line for comfort, so I darkened it to `#a8480a` for headroom).\n406:  **`low`: text `#4a545c` on `#e8eaec` fill.**\n407:  - `#e8eaec` (bg) \u2192 linearized R \u2248 0.8071, G \u2248 0.8228, B \u2248 0.8389 \u2192\n413:  - Contrast of the `#e8eaec` fill itself against the white `.task` card\n416:    distinct shape against a white card. That's why `.priority-select`'s\n429:| 1 | `AddTask`'s `priority-select` defaults to `normal` on mount/reset |\n430:| 2 | `priority-select` in `AddTask`, value sent via `onAdd(title, priority)` \u2192 `api.createTask` |\n431:| 3 | Row's `priority-select` `onChange` \u2192 `onPriorityChange(task.id, value)` \u2192 `api.setPriority`, only priority sent, mirrors title-edit precedent of touching one field |\n436:| 8 | `priority-select` always shows current value as visible text + color, no edit-mode required |\n450:system \u2014 one new CSS class family (`priority-select` + two modifiers)", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013Tdfnwx41SqwCArbmuZVhx", "session_id": "3bc8142f-e811-46af-9f9d-e5b2e1f7a2ad"}}
