{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:05:02Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 158, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "10:> open question #1 (interleaved vs. full 3-tier sort). This design is built\n62:- **Sort is a stable partition applied after the existing filter step**, not\n63:  a general sort. `high` tasks float to the top in their original relative\n67:  (interleaved, only `high` moves). JS's `Array.prototype.sort` has been a\n68:  stable sort in every engine this project targets (Node/V8, all evergreen\n70:  ? 0 : 1`) is sufficient \u2014 no custom stable-sort implementation needed.\n194:const sortedTasks = [...visibleTasks].sort(\n199:`sortedTasks` (not `visibleTasks`) is what gets passed to `<TaskList>`,\n200:directly after the existing filter step (`App.jsx:27-31`) \u2014 sort runs\n281:Order is unchanged from today's id order \u2014 the sort key is `0`/`1` on\n283:stable sort leaves the array exactly as filtering produced it.\n289:the priority sort runs, so it never appears \u2014 a high-priority Done task\n304:Before (D is `high`, sorted to top) \u2192 user selects \"Normal\" in D's row \u2192\n306:`sortedTasks` recomputes on the next render, D falls back to its\n433:| 5 | `sortedTasks` stable partition in `App.jsx`, applied after `visibleTasks`; \"Populated \u2014 AC5 example\" wireframe |\n434:| 6 | Partition key ties (`1`/`1`) when no `high` present \u2192 stable sort is a no-op; \"no `high` tasks\" wireframe |\n435:| 7 | Sort applied to `visibleTasks` (post-filter), not raw `tasks`; \"filter interaction\" wireframe |\n437:| 9 | Sort recomputes on every render from `task.priority`; \"priority changed\" before/after wireframe |\n442:No new sort/filter UI control \u2014 the priority sort is automatic, exactly as\n446:filtering/sorting \u2014 the sort step runs strictly after the existing filter,", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LjFptvrpW4Y99fVsDK6VGf", "session_id": "3bc8142f-e811-46af-9f9d-e5b2e1f7a2ad"}}
