{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:05:08Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 164, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "340\tin this app (unchanged component). The select shows the task's actual\n341\tlast-known-good priority (see \"No optimistic update\" above) rather than\n342\twhatever the user clicked, since it's bound to server state \u2014 no separate\n343\trevert logic to design or build.\n344\t\n345\t### Empty / Loading\n346\t\n347\tUnchanged. `.empty` (per-filter copy) and `.loading` states don't involve\n348\tany task row, so they don't involve priority at all \u2014 no new design\n349\tneeded here.\n350\t\n351\t## Interactive states\n352\t\n353\t- **`priority-select` closed, default (`normal`):** plain bordered control,\n354\t  identical visual weight to `.task-title-input`.\n355\t- **`priority-select` closed, `high`:** solid `#a8480a` fill, white text \u2014\n356\t  the one state in a row designed to actively draw the eye.\n357\t- **`priority-select` closed, `low`:** light `#e8eaec` fill, `#4a545c`\n358\t  text \u2014 visually recessive, consistent with \"low\" meaning \"less urgent\n359\t  than the baseline,\" not \"broken\" or \"hidden.\"\n360\t- **`priority-select` open (dropdown expanded):** native OS/browser\n361\t  rendering for the options list \u2014 not restyled. This app introduces no\n362\t  custom-dropdown component anywhere else, and building one here would be\n363\t  new UI-pattern surface the spec's non-goals don't ask for.\n364\t- **`priority-select` focused:** native browser focus ring, same as every\n365\t  other input/select in this app (no custom `:focus` rule exists\n366\t  anywhere in `App.css` today \u2014 not introducing one here either).\n367\t- **`priority-select` mid-request:** no per-control loading affordance,\n368\t  consistent with round 2's explicit decision that this app has no\n369\t  per-action loading state anywhere (`Done`/`Delete` don't show one\n370\t  either) \u2014 only the shared error banner on failure.\n371\t\n372\t## Accessibility\n373\t\n374\t- **Labels:** `aria-label=\"Priority\"` on `AddTask`'s select,\n375\t  `aria-label={\\`Priority for ${task.title}\\`}` on each row's select \u2014\n376\t  same pattern already used for `Edit`/`Complete`/`Delete`\n377\t  (`TaskList.jsx:74, 89, 91, 95`).\n378\t- **Target size:** `.priority-select`'s padding (`0.4rem 0.6rem` + 1px\n379\t  border) renders at roughly 30\u201332px tall, clearing the ~24px minimum and\n380\t  sitting close to the row's existing `Edit`/`Done`/`Delete` buttons\n381\t  (~34\u201336px per round 2's note) so it doesn't look like a stray smaller\n382\t  control.\n383\t- **Keyboard:** native `<select>` \u2014 full keyboard support (arrow keys to\n384\t  change value, Enter/Space to open, no custom key handling needed). Tab", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Vd1GncNxnDhDoQGrJjtibk", "session_id": "3bc8142f-e811-46af-9f9d-e5b2e1f7a2ad"}}
